  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Warming and drying trend through Sunday; cool/cold valley lows \nwith patchy frost.\n\n-  Increased westerly winds on Monday-Tuesday\n\n-  Low confidence for unsettled weather next weekend\n\nVisible satellite imagery this afternoon is pretty clear over the\nNorthern Rockies, with just some high clouds streaming over the\nIdaho Panhandle and northwest Montana. A ridge of high pressure \nwill continue to build through Sunday, keeping daytime high \ntemperatures about 10-15 degrees above normal under mostly clear \nskies. The ridge flattens out on Monday, becoming westerly, as a\nbroad trough of low pressure moves across western Canada. Westerly\nwinds will increase for Monday and, to a lesser extent, Tuesday \nbefore high pressure again builds for midweek. \n\nModel ensembles are still showing chances for more unsettled\nweather later on Friday into the weekend. While most ensemble\nmembers are on board for a chance, timing and intensity of a \nCanadian trough are topics of disagreement. As a result, \nconfidence remains low on the details of the forecast much beyond\nFriday.",
